<title>UK: Details of 109 mln bls mogas fleet hitting U.S..</title>
<headline>Details of 109 mln bls mogas fleet hitting U.S..</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A fleet of oil tankers loaded with over 900,000 tonnes of European gasoline has begun arriving in the United States, oil traders and ship brokers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>This is the equivalent of 109 million barrels, using a conversion rate of 8.33, and reflects finished and unfinished gasoline, and blending components, they said.</p>
<p>The first tankers are thought to have already discharged their cargo over the last couple of days but the bulk of the armada, which totals nearly 30 ships will be arriving towards the end of January, they said.</p>
<p>The table below gives details of those tankers which sources said have been fixed on the spot market in recent weeks.</p>
<p>It does not include oil company-owned tonnage or vessels on long-term charter.</p>
<p>A typical journey time from Europe to the U.S eastern seaboard inclusive of loading and unloading is estimated by shipbrokers to be around two weeks.</p>
